This standalone window-level keydown listener fires on EVERY lowercase 'p' keystroke while the lightbox is open. It has NO check for whether the user is currently typing in an input. The lightbox contains the face-name <input id="lbFaceNameInput"> (line 1620), which is shown and focused (line 19960-19962: nb.style.display='block'; input.focus()) whenever the user clicks a face box to name a person. The MAIN lightbox keydown handler explicitly bails out for exactly this input (lines 13621-13624: `if (ae && (ae.id === 'lbFaceNameInput' || ae.tagName === 'INPUT' || ae.tagName === 'TEXTAREA')) return;`) and even adds a redundant per-key guard for F (line 13789: `if(e.target && e.target.id === 'lbFaceNameInput') return;`), proving the intended contract is 'don't fire shortcuts while typing in this field'. This standalone 'p' handler is the only one that skips that guard.

